INT. VILLAGE HALL, AMATEUR DRAMATICS REHEARSAL - NIGHT

A cold hall with a stacked-chair smell. Folding table of tea urns. A makeshift stage of pallets.

Four people stand in a loose semicircle: DIRECTOR HILDEGARD OYEGUN-LAMBERT (60s, scarf, a script held aloft), the LEADING LADY DORIS ABERNATHY-OKOYE (50s, hat and gloves already on), the VILLAIN REGINALD TSAI-FAIRBANKS (40s, cape, mustache of black felt), and the STAGEHAND JUNIPER ACHEBE-MOREAU (teen, headphones round her neck).

HILDEGARD
From "Who among you has done this?"

DORIS
Who among you has done this?

REGINALD
I have done nothing.

DORIS
Then why is the knife in your pocket?

REGINALD
(to himself)
Is it the left or the right?

HILDEGARD
The left, Reginald.

REGINALD
The left.

He pulls out a rubber dagger. Dramatic pause. It folds in half.

JUNIPER
(muttering)
Told you not to buy it at the dollar store.

HILDEGARD
Juniper.

JUNIPER
Sorry.

HILDEGARD
(to the room)
Everyone, a short break.

They disperse. Doris heads to the tea urn. Reginald examines the dagger. Hildegard and Juniper stay center stage.

HILDEGARD (CONT'D)
That wasn't the dollar store.

JUNIPER
What?

HILDEGARD
The knife. It's not from the dollar store.

JUNIPER
Then where?

HILDEGARD
It's not the prop knife at all. Reginald brought his own.

JUNIPER
So?

HILDEGARD
This is the prop.

She holds up the folded rubber. Then, slowly, she turns toward Reginald, who is stirring tea. A real blade glints in his pocket as he bends.

Doris sees it. Juniper sees it. Hildegard lowers the script.

HILDEGARD (CONT'D)
(very calmly)
Reginald. Show me the other one.
